==== Power control MCU ====

Since PCB revision v2.6.2 (https://forum.gl-inet.com/t/gl-mifi-gpio-how-to-read-battery-status/7246/6) the power control MCU have a communication channel to the main CPU via a UART at 1200 baud, connected to GPIO 8 (RX) and GPIO 19 (TX).

A soft UART is required to use it.

GL.iNet offers in their firmware the package gl-mifi-mcu with a kernel module for soft UART based in https://github.com/adrianomarto/soft_uart.

The MCU responds to the following commands:



|g| {"T":25.2,"P":86,"C":0} |
|w| watchdog reset! |
|v| version:2.03 time:2019.01.08 |
|s| stop feed dog! |

